\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, I dare believe
\par Thee merciful and true:
\par Thou wilt my guilty soul forgive,
\par My fallen soul renew.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come then for Jesu's sake,
\par And bid my heart be clean;
\par An end of my troubles make,
\par An end of all my sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I will, through grace, I will,
\par I do, return to Thee;
\par Take, empty it, O Lord, and fill
\par My heart with purity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For power I feebly pray:
\par Thy kingdom now restore,
\par To-day, while it is called to-day,
\par And I shall sin no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I cannot wash my heart,
\par But by believing Thee,
\par And waiting for Thy blood to impart
\par The spotless purity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. While at Thy Cross I lie,
\par Jesus, the grace bestow,
\par Now Thy all-cleansing blood apply,
\par And I am white as snow. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

